@startuml UC-69 Create Content Comment - Sequence Diagram
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #000000
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #000000
skinparam ArrowColor #000000
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 280
title UC-69 Create Content Comment — Sequence Diagram

actor "Teacher or Moderator" as User
participant ":CommunityHubDetailPage" as UI
participant ":HubContentController" as CTL
participant ":HubCommentService" as SVC
participant ":LibraryContentRepository" as CONTENTS
participant ":HubCommentRepository" as COMMENTS
database DB

autonumber
User -> UI : Enter the comment text in the comment box of the Community Hub content detail screen
activate UI
User -> UI : Click the send button
UI -> UI : addComment()
UI -> CTL : POST /api/hub/contents/{id}/comments
activate CTL
CTL -> SVC : create(contentId, content, parentCommentId)
activate SVC

SVC -> CONTENTS : findApprovedForHubById(contentId)
activate CONTENTS
CONTENTS -> DB : SELECT * FROM library_contents WHERE id = ? AND status = 'APPROVED' AND deleted_at IS NULL
activate DB
DB --> CONTENTS : row / none
deactivate DB
CONTENTS --> SVC : Optional<LibraryContent>
deactivate CONTENTS
SVC -> SVC : sanitize the comment HTML and check that it is not empty and stays within 200 words

alt the content is no longer published on the Community Hub
  SVC --> CTL : ResourceNotFoundException
  CTL --> UI : HTTP 404
  UI --> User : Show that the content is unavailable and keep the entered text

else the comment text is empty or exceeds 200 words
  SVC --> CTL : IllegalArgumentException
  CTL --> UI : HTTP 400
  UI --> User : Highlight the comment box, show MSG02 and keep the entered text

else the comment cannot be saved
  UI --> User : Show MSG25 and keep the entered comment text

else the content accepts comments and the text is valid
  SVC -> COMMENTS : save(comment)
  activate COMMENTS
  COMMENTS -> DB : INSERT INTO hub_content_comments with library_content_id = ? and parent_comment_id NULL for a root comment
  activate DB
  DB --> COMMENTS : Saved
  deactivate DB
  COMMENTS --> SVC : HubComment
  deactivate COMMENTS
  SVC -> SVC : build the comment view with the author display name, avatar and timestamps
  SVC --> CTL : HubViews.CommentView
  CTL --> UI : HTTP 201 + HubViews.CommentView
  UI --> User : Show MSG08 and append the new comment with its author name and time to the discussion
end

deactivate SVC
deactivate CTL
deactivate UI
@enduml
